# CVE-2026-93687 (braces 3.0.3): genuine, currently unfixed upstream -- no patched
# braces release exists (status "affected", empty fixed version). Recorded as an
# exception rather than treated as a false positive.
#
# Reachability, verified against the installed tree (npm explain braces):
#   @payloadcms/storage-s3 -> @payloadcms/plugin-cloud-storage -> find-node-modules
#   -> findup-sync -> micromatch -> braces
# find-node-modules is declared in plugin-cloud-storage's package.json but is never
# imported anywhere in its published dist, so the chain is installed, not executed.
# The other path (sass -> chokidar 3.x -> braces) is removed by the "sass" ->
# "chokidar" override in package.json, which is why this is the only remaining entry.
#
# Time-boxed: the exp: date makes Trivy report this again after it. Before
# extending, re-run the scan un-ignored and check whether braces, micromatch or the
# Payload storage plugin now ship a fix.
CVE-2026-93687 exp:2026-12-31
